WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.570
John Kramer is back with a brand-new set of
death traps and nefarious intentions, so here's

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.600
everything you need to know before watching
"Saw X".

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.269
Horror movies aren't just reserved for the
spooky season, with freaky films popping up

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:14.540
all-year round.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.029
But there is something about a horror flick
being released around Halloween that gives

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:20.550
it a particularly special feel.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.250
Luckily for gore hounds, "Saw X" will start
the scary celebration with a blood-soaked

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.940
bang, as it's hitting theaters on September
29, 2023.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.430
Interestingly, "Saw X" finds itself sandwiched
between quite a few noteworthy horror titles.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.670
It'll be following in the wake of "The Nun
2," but it's coming out before other creepy

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.680
flicks such as "The Exorcist: Believer" and
"Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:47.950
Basically, Halloween Season 2023 is going
to be an absolute treat for anyone wanting

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:52.530
to celebrate at the theater, and "Saw X" is
sure to deliver the goods when it kicks off

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.770
the frightful festivities.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:59.120
We know the film is actually going to be something
of a prequel -- taking place after the original

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.550
"Saw" movie but before the events of "Saw
2."

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.920
That means we'll be following John Kramer
during his final days, battling cancer and

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.369
searching for some sort of miracle cure.

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:12.700
John's desperation will take him to Mexico,
where he's hoping to sign up for an experimental

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.700
medical procedure.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.220
Unfortunately, John finds out that there's
no actual cure.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.400
The people making lofty promises are all con
artists, and there's no hope for John's health

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.630
below the border.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:26.430
Of course, now that the Jigsaw Killer has
traveled all this way, he isn't going to waste

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.900
the opportunity to murder some people, now
is he?

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.399
Furious at the scammers for taking advantage
of hopeless people, John decides it's time

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:34.420
to play a game.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.140
Soon enough, the folks who lured John to Mexico
with promises of salvation will find themselves

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.740
trapped in a hell of Jigsaw's making and punished
for their sins.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.930
"Let the game begin."

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.159
Going into "Saw X," fans of the series wanted
to know only one thing -- would Tobin Bell

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:51.540
reprise his role as John Kramer?

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.500
The good news is, Bell is indeed coming back.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.110
Remarking on his return, the franchise producers
expressed excitement at Bell's return and

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:03.810
mentioned how the John Kramer character is
a major part of the franchise's success.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:08.380
Director Kevin Greutert agreed with this sentiment,
telling Empire that "Saw X" would focus on

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.759
Jigsaw more than any other film in the series.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:15.750
We'll also see quite a few new faces populating
the screen, with the talented cast including

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:22.150
the likes of Steven Brand, Michael Beach,
Renata Vaca, Paulette Hernandez, Joshua Okamoto,

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:25.930
Octavio Hinojosa, and Synnøve Macody Lund.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:29.550
But will we see any former "Saw" stars returning
alongside Tobin Bell?

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.860
It's entirely possible.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:35.760
Shawnee Smith is definitely returning as John
Kramer apprentice Amanda Young, and for a

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.599
while, there was a rumor that Cary Elwes could
return as serial killer Dr. Lawrence Gordon.

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:44.440
Unfortunately for fans, Elwes told Screen
Rant in April 2023:

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:50.120
"I have no comment one way or the other about
that franchise; I really can't speak to it.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.490
I'm happy for the filmmakers that they continue
to make money, and that it seems to be a financial

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:59.760
bonus for them, I really can't speak to it
because I'm not really involved anymore."

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:05.500
Director Kevin Greutert is no stranger to
the "Saw" franchise, as he helmed 2009's "Saw

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.080
6" and 2010's "Saw 3D."

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.830
While those were his first two feature film
directorial pursuits, he followed them up

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.390
with three more horror thrillers -- "Jessabelle,"
"Visions," and "Jackals."

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.500
Of course, he isn't the only "Saw" alum working
behind the scenes.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.860
Peter Goldfinger and Josh Stolberg have penned
the screenplay, and their credits include

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:28.400
both "Spiral" and "Jigsaw," proving they're
incredibly familiar with the nefarious games

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.940
and sadistic challenges of the "Saw" franchise.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.918
To hear Greutert tell it, "Saw X" is going
to be his greatest contribution to the series yet.

00:03:35.918 --> 00:03:41.069
Back in February 2023, when shooting wrapped
on the movie, Greutert gave fans an update

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:43.489
on the site formerly known as Twitter, saying:

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:47.049
"It was one of the most rewarding and epic
experiences of my life."

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:51.150
Greutert went on to say that he wanted to
use "Saw X" as the title for the new movie.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.450
For diehard fans, Greutert promised the film
would get back to the core of the franchise

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.480
and focus on John Kramer.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.290
Fans will have to decide for themselves if
"Saw X" lives up to Greutert's enthusiasm.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.829
It might be hard to remember the last time
there was a new "Saw" movie because the last

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:10.040
time the franchise came to the big screen,
it delivered a spin-off story.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.160
2021's "Spiral: From the Book of Saw" told
the story of Detective Zeke Banks searching

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.480
for a serial killer clearly inspired by Jigsaw.

00:04:25.043 --> 00:04:26.913
Speaking to The AU Review, he said:

00:04:26.913 --> 00:04:29.452
"This is not the ninth film in the Saw franchise.

00:04:29.452 --> 00:04:32.423
There easily could be a Saw 9 that follows
Jigsaw."

00:04:32.423 --> 00:04:35.813
"Saw X" seems to prove Bousman's remark completely
wrong.

00:04:35.813 --> 00:04:40.133
It implies that "Spiral" was a "Saw" movie
and completely avoids picking up where "Jigsaw"

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.493
left off at the same time.

00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:46.723
"Saw X" is jumping back in time all the way
to the early 2000s when John Kramer is still

00:04:46.723 --> 00:04:52.075
alive and wreaking havoc, so it's safe to
say we won't be seeing Detective Banks in this outing.

00:04:52.075 --> 00:04:56.633
It's disappointing since the twisty ending
of "Spiral" left fans with a serious cliffhanger.

00:04:56.633 --> 00:05:00.672
Undoubtedly, there will be many fans wondering
what would have happened next in Detective

00:05:00.672 --> 00:05:04.943
Banks' journey and if he would have finally
got revenge for what Emmerson did.

00:05:04.943 --> 00:05:08.593
If that's the case, what was the point of
"Spiral" leaving things so open-ended in the

00:05:08.593 --> 00:05:09.593
first place?

00:05:09.593 --> 00:05:13.353
It seems likely that "Spiral" was meant to
kick off a new era for the "Saw" franchise.

00:05:13.353 --> 00:05:17.524
Having "From the Book of Saw" in its title
clearly set "Spiral" apart from the rest of

00:05:17.524 --> 00:05:21.142
the series and implied that there were more
stories like it to tell.

00:05:21.142 --> 00:05:25.103
The plan might have been to expand on Detective
Banks's story and to look at more serial killers

00:05:25.103 --> 00:05:27.073
inspired by Jigsaw's legacy.

00:05:27.073 --> 00:05:30.642
That plan didn't work out because the numbers
didn't support it.

00:05:30.642 --> 00:05:35.223
"Spiral" completely bombed at the box office
in its opening weekend, which definitely dumped

00:05:35.223 --> 00:05:37.702
cold water on the potential for "Spiral 2."

00:05:37.702 --> 00:05:43.612
Now that "Saw X" is taking the series back
to its roots, "The Book of Saw" might officially be closed.

00:05:43.612 --> 00:05:45.153
"Wait, I thought the Jigsaw Killer was dead."

00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:47.052
"Yeah, but if it's another copycat…"

00:05:47.052 --> 00:05:49.153
"It's going to be a sh**show."

00:05:49.153 --> 00:05:53.223
It might come as a surprise that "Saw X" is
traveling back in time to the early 2000s,

00:05:53.223 --> 00:05:55.093
but it really shouldn't.

00:05:55.093 --> 00:05:59.123
The horror genre is well-known for taking
the occasional odd left turn after a series

00:05:59.123 --> 00:06:01.503
has been kicking around for a long time.

00:06:01.503 --> 00:06:05.063
After we sent Jason to space, everything was
on the table.

00:06:05.063 --> 00:06:08.793
Fans of this particular franchise should already
be used to chronological shenanigans.

00:06:08.793 --> 00:06:13.802
For one thing, "Saw 3" and "Saw 4" happen
simultaneously and the viewer only realizes

00:06:13.802 --> 00:06:14.802
it later.

00:06:14.802 --> 00:06:18.963
Piecing together the entire "Saw" franchise
timeline involves more than just watching

00:06:18.963 --> 00:06:20.473
the movies in order.

00:06:20.473 --> 00:06:24.702
Many characters, including the all-important
John Kramer, have their backstories explained

00:06:24.702 --> 00:06:28.723
in flashback sequences only after they've
hung around for several movies.

00:06:28.723 --> 00:06:33.153
There's only one reason that "Saw X" is going
so far back in the timeline, and fans will

00:06:33.153 --> 00:06:34.943
probably agree it's a good one.

00:06:34.943 --> 00:06:39.273
John Kramer, the original Jigsaw, died all
the way back in "Saw 3."

00:06:39.273 --> 00:06:43.552
Since then the franchise has included him
in flashbacks and prequel stories while mostly

00:06:43.552 --> 00:06:45.123
following copycat killers.

00:06:45.123 --> 00:06:49.433
"Saw X" is bringing the franchise back to
where it started by setting its story in the

00:06:49.433 --> 00:06:53.273
past and letting John Kramer return to the
spotlight for real.

00:06:53.273 --> 00:06:57.563
It may be good to know that "Saw X" is in
experienced hands, but regardless of who's

00:06:57.563 --> 00:07:01.802
working on the movie behind the camera, fans
are showing up for the man who's on screen.

00:07:01.802 --> 00:07:05.683
Tobin Bell helped bring Jigsaw to life in
the original "Saw," and he's been the core

00:07:05.683 --> 00:07:07.172
of the franchise ever since.

00:07:07.172 --> 00:07:12.243
Bell has been in every "Saw" movie except
for 2021's "Spiral," and he's clearly excited

00:07:12.243 --> 00:07:14.313
to get a chance to return to the character.

00:07:14.313 --> 00:07:18.223
In an interview with Build, Bell talked about
what has kept him so engaged with the character

00:07:18.223 --> 00:07:20.133
for the past two decades.

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:24.683
"He's got huge dimension as a character.

00:07:24.683 --> 00:07:27.552
He's a bit of a philosopher."

00:07:27.552 --> 00:07:31.103
Bell added that he'd always be willing to
play a character that interested him as much

00:07:31.103 --> 00:07:32.103
as Jigsaw.

00:07:32.103 --> 00:07:36.163
He also talked about the potential for "Saw
X" to introduce the character to audiences

00:07:36.163 --> 00:07:40.873
who were too young to see the original "Saw"
and its immediate sequels in theaters.

00:07:40.873 --> 00:07:44.933
If there really is a huge influx of new fans,
"Saw X" will be just the beginning of a new

00:07:44.933 --> 00:07:47.153
slate of "Saw" movies.

00:07:47.153 --> 00:07:51.093
There are many words that could accurately
describe John Kramer, but "hero" definitely

00:07:51.093 --> 00:07:52.253
isn't one of them.

00:07:52.253 --> 00:07:56.773
As Jigsaw, John has killed more people than
anyone can count, and he's developed some

00:07:56.773 --> 00:08:00.633
of the most gruesome ways to murder people
that the world has ever seen.

00:08:00.633 --> 00:08:04.313
Despite that, "Saw X" does seem to be putting
John into the position of a typical horror

00:08:04.313 --> 00:08:05.353
movie hero.

00:08:05.353 --> 00:08:09.997
In the movie, John goes to Mexico City to
seek specialized treatment for his terminal cancer.

00:08:09.997 --> 00:08:13.593
The people who treat him are scammers who
want to steal his money by convincing him

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.253
they're medical professionals.

00:08:15.253 --> 00:08:19.223
When John realizes that he's been ripped off,
he sets about punishing the scammers with

00:08:19.223 --> 00:08:21.873
his usual assortment of horrifying traps.

00:08:21.873 --> 00:08:26.383
Whether or not that premise goes far enough
to justify John's brutal murders is up to

00:08:26.383 --> 00:08:31.213
the fans, but "Saw X" goes out of its way
to make John the frontman of the movie.

00:08:31.213 --> 00:08:36.773
Speaking about the film at a fan panel Midsummer
Scream 2023, producer Oren Koules said:

00:08:36.773 --> 00:08:39.892
"John Kramer is absolutely the protagonist
in this movie."

00:08:39.892 --> 00:08:44.252
The producer confirmed that what John experiences
makes him the hero of the film.

00:08:44.252 --> 00:08:49.613
Maybe anti-hero would be a more accurate term,
but Koules's point is important.

00:08:49.613 --> 00:08:52.763
Fans who have been dying to see more John
Kramer finally have a movie where he's the

00:08:52.763 --> 00:08:54.523
real lead character.

00:08:54.523 --> 00:08:58.653
2024 marks the 20th anniversary of the first
"Saw" movie.

00:08:58.653 --> 00:09:03.433
Directed by James Wan, "Saw" caught the attention
of so many horror fans because of its no-holds-barred

00:09:03.433 --> 00:09:07.153
approach to on-screen violence and its remarkable
twist ending.

00:09:07.153 --> 00:09:11.893
The franchise has never exactly been a critical
darling, but it kept filling theaters, so

00:09:11.893 --> 00:09:13.483
the series continued.

00:09:13.483 --> 00:09:15.403
But "Saw" has seen better days.

00:09:15.403 --> 00:09:18.843
We've come a long way since the yearly releases
of the late 2000s.

00:09:18.843 --> 00:09:23.233
Nowadays, "Saw" movies are few and far between,
and they aren't guaranteed to be successes.

00:09:23.233 --> 00:09:28.294
"Spiral" had such an abysmal box office performance
that some were wondering if it meant the franchise

00:09:28.294 --> 00:09:29.463
was finally dead.

00:09:29.463 --> 00:09:33.193
"Saw X" proves that there's still some room
for the series to keep going.

00:09:33.193 --> 00:09:36.752
Clearly the people responsible for making
"Saw" movies still believe in them.

00:09:36.752 --> 00:09:40.953
Tobin Bell is still excited by the characters,
and producers and directors are willing to

00:09:40.953 --> 00:09:43.583
put time and money into making a new movie.

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:47.413
On the other hand, "Saw X" could end up being
a swan song for the series.

00:09:47.413 --> 00:09:52.062
One way or another, the future of the entire
franchise rests on how well "Saw X" is received

00:09:52.062 --> 00:09:53.451
when it finally debuts.

00:09:53.451 --> 00:09:55.701
"Oh, yes.

00:09:55.821 --> 00:09:58.271
There will be blood."

00:09:58.271 --> 00:09:59.487
What's in a name?

00:09:59.583 --> 00:10:03.843
"Saw X" might seem like an obvious title choice,
but there's actually a little bit of depth

00:10:03.843 --> 00:10:04.843
to the name.

00:10:04.843 --> 00:10:08.942
It seemingly confirms that "Spiral" was the
ninth "Saw" movie, regardless of what its

00:10:08.942 --> 00:10:10.303
director had to say.

00:10:10.303 --> 00:10:14.033
But this latest installment isn't taking a
cue from "Fast X" with its title either.

00:10:14.033 --> 00:10:18.893
Instead, "Saw X" is borrowing a title formula
from the franchise's early days to make it

00:10:18.893 --> 00:10:23.273
loud and clear that John Kramer has returned
and "Saw" is back in fighting form.

00:10:23.273 --> 00:10:28.046
When "Saw" was just starting, every movie
in the series got a Roman numeral after the title.

00:10:28.046 --> 00:10:33.843
That finally changed with 2010's "Saw 3D,"
which made an ill-fated attempt to bring "Saw"

00:10:33.843 --> 00:10:35.312
into a new dimension.

00:10:35.312 --> 00:10:38.653
Since then, "Jigsaw" and "Spiral" are the
only "Saw" movies we've gotten.

00:10:38.653 --> 00:10:43.812
"Saw X" is calling back to the original films
with its title, and by placing its story right

00:10:43.812 --> 00:10:45.992
back in the good old days of the franchise.

00:10:45.992 --> 00:10:50.302
All the "Saw" movies end up in a grimy warehouse
at one point or another because that's where

00:10:50.302 --> 00:10:52.113
Jigsaw sets up his traps.

00:10:52.113 --> 00:10:56.062
The movies haven't ever spent much time exploring
the city beyond those warehouses.

00:10:56.062 --> 00:11:00.273
Even "Spiral," which spent more time out in
the daylight than any other "Saw" movie, never

00:11:00.273 --> 00:11:01.843
really clarified the setting.

00:11:01.843 --> 00:11:05.923
For all the incredible attention to detail
that "Saw" pays to the intricate backstory

00:11:05.923 --> 00:11:10.153
of its main character and the torturous traps
he invents, the movies never even tell us

00:11:10.153 --> 00:11:11.192
where they take place.

00:11:11.192 --> 00:11:13.653
Don't expect that to be the case with "Saw
X."

00:11:13.653 --> 00:11:17.643
The trend of setting location-agnostic stories
is going out the window with the franchise's

00:11:17.643 --> 00:11:19.052
latest installment.

00:11:19.052 --> 00:11:23.203
In the movie, John heads to Mexico City in
search of cancer treatment, and the city is

00:11:23.203 --> 00:11:25.083
going to play a huge role in the story.

00:11:25.083 --> 00:11:30.153
"Saw X" was shot on location in Mexico City,
so we'll get to see all the sights alongside

00:11:30.153 --> 00:11:32.643
John before the trap-making gets underway.

00:11:32.643 --> 00:11:37.583
Taking John Kramer to Mexico pulls the franchise
out of the U.S. and into a specific location

00:11:37.583 --> 00:11:39.143
for the very first time.

00:11:39.143 --> 00:11:42.963
The change gives the movie a chance to tell
a new kind of story, and it thrilled the people

00:11:42.963 --> 00:11:44.942
who were working on "Saw X."

00:11:44.942 --> 00:11:50.459
Speaking to fans at Midsummer Scream 2023,
"Saw X" production designer Anthony Stabley said:

00:11:50.459 --> 00:11:55.463
"For us from the get-go, we were already winning
because Mexico is so exotic, and John Kramer's

00:11:55.463 --> 00:11:56.986
like a fish out of water."

00:11:56.986 --> 00:12:00.953
Finally pushing John into a space where he's
not in control lets fans see the character

00:12:00.953 --> 00:12:02.023
in a whole new light.

00:12:02.023 --> 00:12:06.153
Also, it makes for a welcome change to the
usual locations where he lets his nefarious

00:12:06.153 --> 00:12:08.312
imagination run wild.

00:12:08.312 --> 00:12:12.302
Director Kevin Greutert knows exactly where
the "Saw" franchise has been before, and he

00:12:12.302 --> 00:12:17.875
wanted to use Mexico City as fuel for telling
a story that "Saw" fans haven't already seen previously.

00:12:17.875 --> 00:12:20.973
Speaking at Midsummer Scream 2023, he said:

00:12:20.973 --> 00:12:25.713
"There's such a mythology, the city is so
amazing, and we can't speak enough about it.

00:12:25.713 --> 00:12:30.583
And just that, there’s a certain creepiness
to it and a certain history, and it just absolutely

00:12:30.583 --> 00:12:31.583
worked for us."

00:12:31.583 --> 00:12:34.533
"It stood the test of time."

00:12:34.533 --> 00:12:39.173
Coming in at one hour and 58 minutes, "Saw
X" is the longest film in the series to date.

00:12:39.173 --> 00:12:42.633
Naturally, that means there will be enough
time to show off the real main attraction

00:12:42.633 --> 00:12:46.493
of the movie and what everyone is here for:
The traps.

00:12:46.493 --> 00:12:51.133
As with every new "Saw" movie, you can expect
"Saw X" to be filled with brand new, hyper-violent

00:12:51.133 --> 00:12:52.133
contraptions.

00:12:52.133 --> 00:12:55.333
The poster for the movie already gives a hint
of what to expect.

00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:59.913
It shows someone locked into a set of creepy
goggles that have tubes connected to the eyes.

00:12:59.913 --> 00:13:03.733
Whatever the device is meant to do, watching
it in action will probably make you cringe

00:13:03.733 --> 00:13:05.043
and have sympathy pains.

00:13:05.043 --> 00:13:10.171
The official "Saw X" trailer also gives a
few brief glances at John's inventions in the movie.

00:13:10.171 --> 00:13:13.913
It shows a group of people chained up inside
a classic "Saw" warehouse.

00:13:13.913 --> 00:13:16.305
One woman appears to have a saw blade set
up in front of her neck.

00:13:16.305 --> 00:13:20.573
A panicked man is strapped into some kind
of modified electric chair.

00:13:20.573 --> 00:13:25.573
In a different shot, we can see a Jigsaw puppet
wheeling out surgical supplies to John's victims.

00:13:25.573 --> 00:13:30.752
From the little we've seen, "Saw X" looks
to be as gruesome as its predecessors.

00:13:30.752 --> 00:13:35.743
Every time a series introduces a new prequel,
the chances for retconning skyrocket.

00:13:35.743 --> 00:13:39.853
Altering a story's past is one of the best
ways to dramatically change its future.

00:13:39.853 --> 00:13:44.807
On the surface, "Saw X" seems like a perfect
opportunity for the "Saw" canon to reinvent itself.

00:13:44.807 --> 00:13:47.033
Maybe John Kramer had a secret child.

00:13:47.033 --> 00:13:51.213
Or perhaps his time in Mexico City gave him
the perfect strategy for faking his death

00:13:51.213 --> 00:13:54.172
at the end of "Saw 3," and he's been alive
all this time.

00:13:54.172 --> 00:13:59.619
"Saw X" could hit the restart button for the
franchise in any number of ways, but it probably won't.

00:13:59.619 --> 00:14:03.933
If the franchise really wanted to take things
in a different direction, it probably wouldn't

00:14:03.933 --> 00:14:06.963
be diving back into John Kramer's past at
all.

00:14:06.963 --> 00:14:11.633
John has been dead for the majority of the
franchise's existence at this point, so retconning

00:14:11.633 --> 00:14:15.133
his death would completely ruin the story
of most of the movies.

00:14:15.133 --> 00:14:19.043
Aside from John's death, there's really no
big event in the series that is even remotely

00:14:19.043 --> 00:14:20.812
asking for a retcon.

00:14:20.812 --> 00:14:24.802
It seems pretty safe to assume that "Saw X"
is going back in time just to give us another

00:14:24.802 --> 00:14:29.492
Jigsaw story, and it probably won't do anything
that impacts what the rest of the series has

00:14:29.492 --> 00:14:30.802
already established.

00:14:30.802 --> 00:14:35.682
The latest installment's director, Kevin Greutert,
thinks that the franchise could continue,

00:14:35.682 --> 00:14:37.573
but he's just not entirely sure how.

00:14:37.573 --> 00:14:38.903
Speaking to SFX, he said:

00:14:38.903 --> 00:14:43.033
"There's no obvious direction to go after
this film, but I think there probably will

00:14:43.033 --> 00:14:46.432
be more Saw movies, particularly if this one
is successful."

00:14:46.432 --> 00:14:48.872
"I'm long gone from this world."

00:14:48.872 --> 00:14:53.362
Considering that the original "Saw" came out
in 2004, there's now an entire generation

00:14:53.362 --> 00:14:56.163
of moviegoers who missed out on the franchise's
heyday.

00:14:56.163 --> 00:14:59.872
"Saw" made enough of a cultural impact that
even people who were young enough to miss

00:14:59.872 --> 00:15:03.603
actually seeing the movie probably knew a
little about its premise.

00:15:03.603 --> 00:15:07.872
There's an extensive backlog of "Saw" movies
for new fans to brush up on, but it's probably

00:15:07.872 --> 00:15:12.343
not necessary to see them all before showing
up at the theater for "Saw X."

00:15:12.343 --> 00:15:15.823
Anyone who's looking for the bare minimum
catch-up story before "Saw X" should at least

00:15:15.823 --> 00:15:17.453
watch the original movie.

00:15:17.453 --> 00:15:22.083
It takes place right before the events of
"Saw X," but to really get the full context,

00:15:22.083 --> 00:15:27.062
it's also worth watching "Saw 2" and "Saw
3," which carry the story through to the death

00:15:27.062 --> 00:15:28.432
of John Kramer.

00:15:28.432 --> 00:15:32.922
After that, watching "Saw 4" all the way through
to "Jigsaw" will give fans the fullest possible

00:15:32.922 --> 00:15:36.639
picture of John's story and the lives of the
killers he inspired.

00:15:36.639 --> 00:15:41.491
Beyond that, true completists can check out
"Spiral," if they haven't already.

